## 6. Routing & Guards

All feature routes are lazy-loaded via `loadComponent` or `loadChildren`. Attach roles
through route `data` and read them in `role.guard.ts`.

| Path | Component area | Guards | Allowed roles |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `/login` | auth | — | anonymous |
| `/register`, `/forgot-password` | auth | — | anonymous |
| `/platform` | super-admin dashboard | auth, role | `SysAdmin` |
| `/platform/organizations` | organizations list/create/detail | auth, role | `SysAdmin` |
| `/platform/org-admins` | Org-Admin creator | auth, role | `SysAdmin` |
| `/dashboard` | role-aware dashboard redirect | auth | all authenticated |
| `/users` | user & staff listings, create, detail | auth, role, tenant | `OrgAdmin` |
| `/categories` | category listing & create | auth, role, tenant | `OrgAdmin`, `Instructor` |
| `/trainings` | training create, category view, assign | auth, role, tenant | `OrgAdmin`, `Instructor` |
| `/processing` | material upload & design | auth, role, tenant | `OrgAdmin`, `Instructor` |
| `/staff-ops` | trainee ops, messaging, assignment | auth, role, tenant | `Instructor` |
| `/portal` | learner training & scores | auth, role, tenant | `Learner` |
| `**` | not-found | — | any |

- `auth.guard.ts` redirects unauthenticated users to `/login` with a `returnUrl`.
- `role.guard.ts` redirects authorized-but-wrong-role users to their own dashboard and
  raises a toast. It must never leave the user on a blank screen.
- `tenant.guard.ts` rejects any route whose `:organizationId` parameter does not match
  `activeOrganizationId`, unless the user is `SysAdmin`.
- `/dashboard` resolves to the correct dashboard by role: `SysAdmin` → `/platform`,
  `OrgAdmin` and `Instructor` → their dashboard, `Learner` → `/portal`.

